  "accepted_scope": "For the exact six-relation R(alpha,beta), the nonzero homogeneous completely prime linear ideal I=(x3-x1,x4-x2) is strictly below R+, and the exact quotient is B(P1,O(1),sigma), sigma[s:t]=[s+beta*t:beta*s+t]. The unital graded surjection has positive-dimensional projective target, Hilbert series (1-z)^(-2) and GK-dimension 2. This fully refutes both literal assertions printed in the 2010 OWR report and 2012 Rogalski–Sierra article for all prescribed algebraically independent parameters. The presentation theorem works over every field for beta^2!=1 and arbitrary alpha; in characteristic two it does not identify the journal geometric family, whose fractional parameter conversion is used only in characteristic different from two. No prime classification, embedding, common graded quotient ring or surface-dimensional image is claimed.",
  "priority_summary": "Historical priority remains UNRESOLVED. Classical quantum/Jordan-plane, degree-reduction, graded-twist and THCR machinery is credited. Two independently positioned bounded primary-source audits verified no full matching predecessor in inspected passages. Nevins–Sierra arXiv:1206.0760v1 page 25 and v2 pages 28–29 repeat the contrary no-map assertion; their canonical-factor/moduli theorems need extra hypotheses. The inspected preprint versions, including v2's 14 April 2014 arXiv revision and internal 15 November 2018 date, are distinguished from the unread journal body. Campbell's baseline infinitesimal deformations and function skew fields of another family are not this exact generic algebra's homomorphic curve quotient. Older books/papers, unread versions, incomplete citation coverage and nonindexed work remain gaps. No firstness, certified novelty, exhaustive absence or current worldwide-open claim.",
